@*
    Privacy Policy — English text. Counterpart of _PrivacyBody.tr.cshtml.

    Kept as a whole document rather than resx keys on purpose: legal text is reviewed
    section by section, sentences depend on one another, and the two language versions
    may legitimately diverge in structure over time.

    Substantive parity with the Turkish version is REQUIRED. Both must always state: the
    data controller, where data is hosted (Hetzner, Germany; not Firebase), every
    third-party SDK (Firebase Auth/Analytics/Crashlytics/Cloud Messaging, RevenueCat),
    that no advertising identifier (IDFA) is used and no ad tracking takes place, the
    30-day log retention, search history, sharing visibility, content reports, the
    export/deletion rights, and the last-updated date (rendered by Privacy.cshtml from
    the "privacy.lastUpdated" resource). Verified against the code on 2026-10-18.
*@
<p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
    This policy explains what personal data we process when you use the Somine iPhone app (the
    &quot;App&quot;) and the somineapp.com website, why we process it, where we keep it, and what
    rights you have over it. We don&apos;t show ads, we don&apos;t sell your data, and we don&apos;t
    track you across other apps.
</p>

<div class="bg-[#E8F1EF] rounded-2xl p-6 border border-[#688E8B]/10">
    <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">
        Data controller
    </h3>
    <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        For the purposes of the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and Turkey&apos;s Personal
        Data Protection Law No. 6698 (KVKK), the data controller is
        <strong class="text-gray-900">Gökmen Küçük (GSO Studio)</strong>. Contact:
        <a href="mailto:destek@somineapp.com" class="text-[#688E8B] hover:underline font-medium">destek@somineapp.com</a>
        (support@somineapp.com and abuse@somineapp.com reach the same inbox).
    </p>
</div>

<div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-[#688E8B]/10 text-[#688E8B] flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">1</span>
        What we collect
    </h2>
    <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-500">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Account details:</strong> You can only sign in with Apple or
                Google. From them we receive your name, your email address (Apple&apos;s relay address if you
                choose &quot;Hide My Email&quot;) and your profile photo, if you have one. Your account also
                holds the username and display name you choose, any profile photo you upload, and your
                device&apos;s time zone so reminders fire at the right time.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">What you save:</strong> Links, notes, images you upload,
                collections, favorites and reminders. When you save a link we fetch the page&apos;s public
                title, description and image to show a preview. To bring forgotten saves back to you, we
                also record when you last opened an item and how many times.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Search history:</strong> Your last 10 searches are stored on
                our server so they&apos;re available on all your devices. They are deleted with your account.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Sharing, blocking and reports:</strong> Which collections you
                share and with whom, public links you create, users you block, and reports you submit
                (reason, optional note, and the collection and user concerned).
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Notification token:</strong> So we can send you push
                notifications, your device&apos;s push token, platform and language are stored on our server.
                They are deleted when you sign out or delete your account.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Subscription status:</strong> Whether Premium is active, which
                plan, and when it expires. Your payment details (card etc.) never reach us; Apple handles payment.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Usage and diagnostics:</strong> Statistics such as which
                screens are opened and which features are used (Firebase Analytics), and, when the app
                crashes, the crash log, device model and iOS version (Firebase Crashlytics). This data is
                not linked to your account identity.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Security and error logs:</strong> For every request to our
                server we log the IP address, device/browser information (user agent), request path, status
                code, duration and, if you&apos;re signed in, your user ID. For your sign-in sessions we keep
                the device name, IP address and user agent. These logs exist for security and debugging and
                are deleted after <strong class="text-gray-900">30 days</strong>.
            </div>
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mt-4">
        <strong class="text-gray-900">What we don&apos;t collect:</strong> your location (even when the app
        shows a saved place on a map, your location isn&apos;t sent to us), your contacts, your advertising
        identifier (IDFA), or Face ID data. Face ID checks happen entirely on your device; no biometric
        data ever reaches us.
    </p>
</div>

<div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-[#688E8B]/10 text-[#688E8B] flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">2</span>
        Why we use it
    </h2>
    <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-500">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">To run the service:</strong> creating your account, syncing
                your saves across devices, sharing, reminders and notifications, and recognising Premium.
                (Legal basis: performance of our contract with you.)
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Security and moderation:</strong> preventing abuse, reviewing
                reports, and finding and fixing bugs. (Legal basis: legitimate interests.)
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Improving the product:</strong> seeing, in aggregate, which
                features get used. (Legal basis: legitimate interests.)
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Legal obligations:</strong> responding to lawful requests from
                the authorities. (Legal basis: legal obligation.)
            </div>
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mt-4">
        We never use your data for advertising, profiling or sale.
    </p>
</div>

<div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-[#688E8B]/10 text-[#688E8B] flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">3</span>
        Where your data is stored
    </h2>
    <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Your account, your saves, the images you upload and the other data listed above are stored in a
        PostgreSQL database on our own servers in Hetzner&apos;s data center in
        <strong class="text-gray-900">Nuremberg, Germany (EU)</strong>. Your content is not stored in Firebase.
    </p>
    <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
        The service providers listed below (Google/Firebase, RevenueCat, Apple) may process the data
        they handle in countries outside the EU and Turkey, including the United States. This is necessary
        for the service to work, and we only share with each provider what it needs for its own function.
    </p>
</div>

<div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-[#688E8B]/10 text-[#688E8B] flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">4</span>
        What others see when you share
    </h2>
    <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-500">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Sharing with a person:</strong> when you send someone a
                collection, they see your display name, your username and the collection&apos;s contents.
                Other users can send you shares using your username.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Public links:</strong> anyone who has the link can see the
                collection and your display name, even without an account. You can revoke a link at any
                time and it stops working immediately. Collections in the Hidden Vault can&apos;t have a
                public link.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">When you report something:</strong> the report is stored on
                our server and emailed to our moderator, who reviews it within 24 hours. The person you
                report never sees who reported them. Blocking someone doesn&apos;t notify them either.
            </div>
        </li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-[#688E8B]/10 text-[#688E8B] flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">5</span>
        Service providers we use
    </h2>
    <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-500">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Firebase Authentication (Google):</strong> verifies Sign in
                with Apple and Google. Your name, email address and a user ID are held here.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Firebase Analytics (Google):</strong> shows us, in aggregate,
                how the app is used. <strong class="text-gray-900">No advertising identifier (IDFA) is used
                and no tracking for advertising purposes takes place</strong>, which is why the app never asks
                for tracking permission (App Tracking Transparency).
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Firebase Crashlytics (Google):</strong> collects the crash
                log, device model and iOS version when the app crashes, purely so we can fix bugs.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Firebase Cloud Messaging (Google):</strong> delivers
                notifications such as share requests and reminders to your device, using your device&apos;s
                push token.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">RevenueCat:</strong> verifies your App Store subscription and
                tells us whether Premium is active. RevenueCat receives your user ID and purchase history,
                not your payment details.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Apple (App Store, Sign in with Apple) and Google (Sign in with
                Google):</strong> sign-in and payment are handled by these companies under their own privacy
                policies.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Hetzner:</strong> the German data center that hosts our
                servers. It provides the infrastructure and does not access your data.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Error monitoring:</strong> we may use Sentry to monitor server
                errors. If so, Sentry receives error details only; sending personal data is switched off.
            </div>
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mt-4">
        We don&apos;t share data with anyone else. If the law requires it, we disclose only what a lawful
        request from the authorities covers.
    </p>
</div>

<div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-[#688E8B]/10 text-[#688E8B] flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">6</span>
        Cookies
    </h2>
    <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        <strong class="text-gray-900">The app doesn&apos;t use cookies</strong>, so it has no cookie settings either.
    </p>
    <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-gray-900">somineapp.com</strong> uses a strictly necessary cookie that remembers your
        language choice for a year. Google Analytics cookies (names starting with
        <span class="font-mono text-xs">_ga</span>) are used for visitor statistics <strong class="text-gray-900">only if you
        consent</strong>; if you decline they are not loaded. You can change your choice at any time in the
        <a href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="window.somineCookiePrefs &amp;&amp; window.somineCookiePrefs()" class="underline">cookie preferences</a>.
    </p>
</div>

<div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-[#688E8B]/10 text-[#688E8B] flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">7</span>
        How long we keep it
    </h2>
    <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-500">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            Account details, saves, collections, shares, reminders, notifications, search history, blocks
            and reports: for as long as your account exists. They are deleted immediately when you delete
            your account.
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            An item you delete first moves to <em>Recently Deleted</em>; it is erased for good when you delete
            it from there or delete your account.
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            Notification token: deleted when you sign out or delete your account.
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            Security and error logs (IP address, user agent): 30 days.
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            Data held by Firebase Analytics, Crashlytics and RevenueCat follows those providers&apos;
            retention periods.
        </li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-[#688E8B]/10 text-[#688E8B] flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">8</span>
        Security
    </h2>
    <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
        All traffic between the app and our server is encrypted with HTTPS (TLS). Your session keys are
        kept in the iOS Keychain on your device. Collections in the Hidden Vault aren&apos;t downloaded to
        your device until you unlock them with Face ID, and they never appear in the widget or in
        notifications. Even so, no transmission over the internet can be guaranteed 100% secure.
    </p>
</div>

<div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-[#688E8B]/10 text-[#688E8B] flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">9</span>
        Your rights
    </h2>
    <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Under the GDPR and Article 11 of the KVKK you have the right to:
    </p>
    <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-500">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Access:</strong> find out what data we hold about you and get a copy.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Export:</strong> download all your saves and collections as
                JSON or CSV from Profile &gt; <em>Export your data</em> (free).
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Correction:</strong> change your name, username and profile
                photo in Profile &gt; <em>Account Info</em>.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Deletion:</strong> delete your account and all your data
                permanently and immediately from Profile &gt; <em>Account Info</em> &gt; <em>Delete
                Account</em>. This erases your data on our server, your Firebase sign-in account and your
                notification token, and, if you signed in with Apple, revokes Somine&apos;s Apple sign-in
                authorization. See the
                <a href="/delete-account" class="text-[#688E8B] hover:underline font-medium">Account Deletion</a>
                page for details. Deleting your account does not cancel an App Store subscription; cancel
                that separately in your iPhone&apos;s Settings &gt; [your name] &gt; Subscriptions.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Object and restrict:</strong> object to processing based on
                legitimate interests, ask which third parties received your data, and challenge outcomes
                that work against you.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#688E8B] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
                <strong class="text-gray-900">Complain:</strong> if you&apos;re not satisfied with our answer,
                you can lodge a complaint with the data protection authority in your EU country or, in
                Turkey, with the Personal Data Protection Board (kvkk.gov.tr).
            </div>
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mt-4">
        Send requests to
        <a href="mailto:destek@somineapp.com" class="text-[#688E8B] hover:underline font-medium">destek@somineapp.com</a>.
        We reply within 30 days at the latest.
    </p>
</div>

<div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-[#688E8B]/10 text-[#688E8B] flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">10</span>
        Age requirement
    </h2>
    <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
        Somine is for people aged 13 and over. It is not directed at children under 13, and we don&apos;t
        knowingly collect data from them. If you learn that a child under 13 has created an account, let
        us know and we&apos;ll delete the account and its data.
    </p>
</div>

<div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-[#688E8B]/10 text-[#688E8B] flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">11</span>
        Changes to this policy
    </h2>
    <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
        We update this policy as the app changes. If a change is significant, we&apos;ll tell you in the
        app. The date of the current version is shown in the &quot;Last updated&quot; line at the top of
        this page.
    </p>
</div>

